    "text": "In February 2020 the price of Maize (white) in Quarry Gate (no coordinates) had risen 57.2% over 12 months, which is unusual for this market (robust z +3.6; higher than all 84 earlier 12-month changes). It lasted 3 months. Few comparable markets were unusually high at the time. Too few other foods in the same market could be assessed. This pattern is consistent with local supply or market-access disruption, but the data integrated here cannot establish which, if any, was responsible. It cannot assess weather-related production shock, policy intervention or transmission of international prices."
